2025-10-08 12:28:41,537 [WARNING] Skipped idx=165: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='The pro-apoptotic TAp73 isoforms, specifically TAp73α and TAp73β, have been identified in humans. These isoforms are regulated by the extrinsic P1 promoter, and their expression can be reduced due to hypermethylation of this promoter, which is an epigenetic mechanism of transcriptional control. This reduction in TAp73 mRNA levels is relatively infrequent, as observed in the study of 102 primary non-small cell lung carcinomas (NSCLCs). The intrinsic P2 promoter, on the other hand, controls the expression of the anti-apoptotic ΔNp73 isoform, and its hypomethylation is associated with the over-expression of ΔNp73 mRNA, particularly in squamous cell carcinomas. This over-expression is a frequent event and may be a passive consequence of global DNA hypomethylation, as indicated by the strong correlation with LINE-1 element hypomethylation.'
